Description: Boswas OS Control Center, Security Center and Software Center
 The settings hub of Boswas OS (KDE Plasma). One window with a page per
 area, each showing the state of the device as the system reports it,
 offering the actions of that area, and opening the matching KDE settings
 modules (kcmshell6) for everything configured there:
 .
  * Personalization: Boswas desktop presets (boswas-preset) and the KDE
    appearance modules
  * Network: connections, addresses, Wi-Fi radio (NetworkManager)
  * Storage: disks, file systems, and freeing space
  * Hardware & Drivers: PCI and USB devices, their drivers, and missing
    firmware with the Debian package that provides it
  * Boswas Software Center: installed applications; Debian packages from the
    signed repositories, Flatpak applications and AppImages; files routed to
    the right installer by their content
  * Windows Compatibility: runtime health and the Compatibility Manager
  * Android: the optional Waydroid runtime (boswas-android), Android apps and
    APK files
  * Boswas Security Center: the local posture checks of boswas-cli and the
    device agent's state, as Secure, Warning, Attention or Error
  * Boswas Update Center: automatic updates, pending updates, check for and
    install updates
  * Bluetooth, Display, Sound, Power, Users, Devices, Privacy and System
    pages, About Boswas OS with a system overview, and in live sessions a way
    to restart into the installer
 .
 Control Center runs as the desktop user and never as root. It starts only
 a fixed list of programs, each with a validated argument list and a
 timeout, and never through a shell. Administrator operations go only to
 the Boswas system helper (boswas-sysops) through polkit, with an operation
 from a fixed list, and only after the user clicked and confirmed.
